WEBVTT

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:14.870
Operator, operator, operator, operator, I've been ringing Murray Hill 3-5-0-9-7 for the last time.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.260
and the line is always busy.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:17.440
Will you ring it for me, please?

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.300
Murray 5097.

00:02:19.900 --> 00:02:22.100
The husband's office.

00:02:22.320 --> 00:02:23.580
He should have been home hours ago.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:24.880
I can't think what's keeping him

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:26.720
or why that ridiculous wire should be busy.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.940
They always close that office at 6 o'clock.

00:02:32.172 --> 00:02:32.672
Thank you.

00:02:40.396 --> 00:02:41.116
Stevenson, please.

00:02:41.804 --> 00:02:43.484
I want to speak to Mr. Henry Stevenson.

00:02:43.484 --> 00:02:44.124
Oh, George.

00:02:44.908 --> 00:02:46.708
Hello, who is this? What number am I calling?

00:02:50.572 --> 00:02:53.152
Excuse me, what's going on here? I'm using this wire.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.260
You've just given me a wrong number.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:02.200
I'm sorry, madam.

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:03.480
What number were you calling?

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:06.220
Why, I was calling Murray Hill 35097.

00:04:06.220 --> 00:04:07.300
That's my husband's office.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:10.400
And instead, I was cut into some other number that you dialed.

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:11.780
The wires must have crossed or something.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:14.980
And I've just heard the most dreadful thing, a murder.

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:15.620
Yes, madam.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:19.000
And now I want you to get that wrong number back for me at once.

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:20.080
I'm sorry, madam.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:21.080
I do not understand.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.560
You dialed a number for me just a moment ago.

00:04:24.720 --> 00:04:26.460
Murray Hill 35097.

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.720
It was busy for so long, and I asked you to get it, and you did.

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:33.470
And then those horrible men came on.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:35.670
Well, it's unnerved me dreadfully.

00:04:35.810 --> 00:04:36.630
I'm an invalid, you know.

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:38.350
I will connect you with the chief operator.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:38.990
Please.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.700
Oh, chief operator, I'm an invalid.

00:04:55.920 --> 00:04:58.560
And I've just had a dreadful shock tonight over the telephone.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:04:59.980
And I'm very anxious to trace the...

00:05:00.860 --> 00:05:06.760
It was about a murder, a terrible, cold-butted murder of a poor, innocent woman tonight at 11.15.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.690
I was trying to reach my husband's office.

00:05:09.930 --> 00:05:12.390
He should have been home hours and hours ago.

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:13.730
I'm all alone tonight.

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:17.150
My nurse heads the night off because my husband had promised.

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:19.990
As a matter of fact, he'd sworn he'd be home by 6 o'clock.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:23.100
I don't know any of the neighbors, as we live permanently in Chicago.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:27.350
Well, it so happens that the couple I have working for me had some important date or other.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:28.930
I don't know, a movie, I suppose.

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:29.970
They said it was...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.960
promised them three weeks ago you could have thought they'd at least have checked with me before

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:39.300
leaving had some realization of my condition but i've been ringing and ringing the bell for nearly

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:45.100
an hour hoping they'd come back or something and there isn't a sound downstairs not a sound

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:49.280
yes madam so as i say when i kept getting the busy signal in my husband's office i

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:54.620
naturally dialed the operator and told her to try it and she did and then out of a clear sky i

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:59.800
was cut into this ghastly conversation between two killers and now i'd like you to trace it for me at

00:05:59.800 --> 00:05:59.900
work.

00:06:02.300 --> 00:06:03.140
Depends on what?

00:06:03.820 --> 00:06:04.820
Parties have stopped talking.

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:07.790
Talking to each other by now.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:09.410
It was just a short call.

00:06:09.800 --> 00:06:11.460
They weren't exactly gossiping.

00:06:12.460 --> 00:06:13.300
They're having this call.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:13.780
Reason?

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:17.200
Do I have to have a reason when I overheard two murderers?

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:17.940
Isn't it obvious?

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:19.860
Now look here, my good woman.

00:06:20.080 --> 00:06:21.620
You probably don't understand.

00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:27.020
But a human being, a woman, is going to be killed somewhere, somewhere in this very city.

00:06:27.240 --> 00:06:29.160
And this murder is going to take place tonight.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:29.920
Do you hear me tonight?

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.000
Tonight at 11.15. Now, isn't that a good enough reason?

00:06:33.820 --> 00:06:37.140
I understand, madam, but I would suggest that you turn this information...

00:06:38.020 --> 00:06:40.640
Oh, for heaven's sakes, all this idiotic red tape.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.520
You just sit there and let people die.

00:06:42.780 --> 00:06:53.040
Give me the police.

00:06:53.200 --> 00:06:55.060
Yes, I'm in the police department.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:59.540
Tick-tock, tick-tock. Listen to the big tick-tock.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:00.880
Isn't that nice?

00:07:02.180 --> 00:07:02.960
